        "description": "<p>Since this will be the <em>only</em> source of this process on the Internet<sup id=\"fnref:1\"><a href=\"#fn:1\" class=\"footnote-ref\" role=\"doc-noteref\">1</a></sup>, I figured I'd document a quick fan swap I did on a piece of test/reference equipment I'm running in my <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3BBxCn4mY5Y\">Atomic Clock Tower</a>.</p>\n<figure class=\"insert-image\"><img src=\"https://www.jeffgeerling.com/blog/2026/noctua-fan-swap-calnex-rb-gps-frequency-reference/calnex-rb-gps-frequency-reference-open.jpeg\"\n\t\t\talt=\"Calnex Rb/GPS Frequency Reference open on workbench\" width=\"700\" height=\"auto\">\n</figure>\n\n<p>I took my Torx T10 screwdriver and popped off the top cover. The screws required some force to loosen, as they were all secured with Loctite.</p>\n<p>The inside is simple and serviceable. There's a <a href=\"https://www.rebes.net/folder/Spectratime/iSync_GRClok-1500_Spec.pdf\">SpectraTime GRClok-1500</a>, with an integrated timing-grade GPS module, and a stabilized 10 MHz ou",
